#' jjscatterstats Test Datasets
#'
#' Simulated clinicopathological datasets used to exercise the
#' \code{\link{jjscatterstats}} scatter-plot analysis. Each one covers a different
#' correlation scenario a pathologist or clinical researcher would meet: routine
#' laboratory panels, tumour biomarker pairs, gene/protein expression, longitudinal
#' treatment response, survival-linked markers, and a deliberately tiny sample for
#' small-n behaviour.
#'
#' These are synthetic data generated by the scripts in \code{data-raw/}. They are
#' for demonstration and testing only and must not be used to draw clinical or
#' biological conclusions.
#'
#' @name jjscatterstats_datasets
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @seealso \code{\link{jjscatterstats}}
NULL

#' Clinical Laboratory Panel Test Dataset
#'
#' Simulated routine laboratory values with correlated metabolic markers, for
#' testing Pearson/Spearman correlation, grouping by clinical category, and
#' marginal distributions.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 180 observations and 13 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{patient_id}{Integer. Unique patient identifier (1-180)}
#'   \item{diagnosis}{Character. Clinical diagnosis group}
#'   \item{glucose}{Numeric. Fasting glucose, mg/dL (40-215)}
#'   \item{hemoglobin_a1c}{Numeric. HbA1c, percent (3.0-10.3)}
#'   \item{cholesterol}{Numeric. Total cholesterol, mg/dL (120-328)}
#'   \item{triglycerides}{Numeric. Triglycerides, mg/dL (50-283)}
#'   \item{hdl_cholesterol}{Numeric. HDL cholesterol, mg/dL (32.5-78.4)}
#'   \item{bmi}{Numeric. Body mass index, kg/m^2 (11.4-36.9)}
#'   \item{systolic_bp}{Numeric. Systolic blood pressure, mmHg (90-152)}
#'   \item{age}{Numeric. Age in years (28-103)}
#'   \item{age_group}{Factor. Age band ("Young (<45)", "Middle (45-65)", "Senior (>65)"); 1 missing value}
#'   \item{bmi_category}{Factor. BMI band ("Normal", "Overweight", "Obese")}
#'   \item{gender}{Character. Patient gender}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_clinical)
"jjscatterstats_clinical"

#' Gene and Protein Expression Test Dataset
#'
#' Simulated tumour expression profiles with correlated gene- and protein-level
#' measurements across cancer types, for testing correlation with a categorical
#' split and colour/shape aesthetic mappings.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 200 observations and 14 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{sample_id}{Integer. Unique sample identifier (1-200)}
#'   \item{cancer_type}{Character. Tumour type}
#'   \item{stage}{Character. Disease stage}
#'   \item{gene_a_expression}{Numeric. Gene A expression, log2 scale (3.9-11.9)}
#'   \item{gene_b_expression}{Numeric. Gene B expression, log2 scale (3.4-12.6)}
#'   \item{oncogene_expression}{Numeric. Oncogene expression, log2 scale (4.0-15.5)}
#'   \item{tumor_suppressor_expression}{Numeric. Tumour-suppressor expression, log2 scale (3.0-13.0)}
#'   \item{ki67_protein}{Numeric. Ki-67 labelling index, percent (0-56.2)}
#'   \item{pcna_protein}{Numeric. PCNA labelling index, percent (5.0-44.9)}
#'   \item{pdl1_expression}{Numeric. PD-L1 tumour proportion score, percent (0-45.2)}
#'   \item{til_score}{Numeric. Tumour-infiltrating lymphocyte score, percent (0-83.6)}
#'   \item{mutation_burden}{Numeric. Tumour mutational burden, mutations/Mb (0-25.1)}
#'   \item{histology}{Character. Histological subtype}
#'   \item{grade}{Character. Histological grade}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_expression)
"jjscatterstats_expression"

#' Minimal Scatter Plot Test Dataset
#'
#' A deliberately small sample (n = 30) for exercising small-sample behaviour:
#' wide confidence intervals, sparse grouped panels, and the guards that fire when
#' a correlation has too few complete pairs.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 30 observations and 7 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{id}{Integer. Row identifier (1-30)}
#'   \item{x_var}{Numeric. Generic x-axis measurement (12.6-81.7)}
#'   \item{y_var}{Numeric. Generic y-axis measurement (1.3-50.8)}
#'   \item{group}{Character. Two-level grouping variable}
#'   \item{category}{Character. Secondary categorical variable}
#'   \item{measurement}{Numeric. Additional continuous measurement (67.2-130.7)}
#'   \item{score}{Numeric. Additional continuous score (14.3-94.3)}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_small)
"jjscatterstats_small"

#' Survival Biomarker Test Dataset
#'
#' Simulated biomarker measurements paired with time-to-event outcomes, for
#' testing correlation between a continuous marker and survival time, split by
#' stage or treatment.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 160 observations and 13 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{patient_id}{Integer. Unique patient identifier (1-160)}
#'   \item{disease_stage}{Character. Disease stage}
#'   \item{treatment}{Character. Treatment received}
#'   \item{ki67_index}{Numeric. Ki-67 proliferation index, percent (5.0-87.4)}
#'   \item{pdl1_score}{Numeric. PD-L1 score, percent (0-85.2)}
#'   \item{age}{Numeric. Age in years (33-99)}
#'   \item{bmi}{Numeric. Body mass index, kg/m^2 (18.0-41.3)}
#'   \item{age_category}{Factor. Age band ("<50", "50-70", ">70")}
#'   \item{performance_status}{Character. ECOG performance status}
#'   \item{survival_months}{Numeric. Overall survival, months (0.8-121.8)}
#'   \item{pfs_months}{Numeric. Progression-free survival, months (1.0-68.7)}
#'   \item{response_score}{Numeric. Treatment response score (6.1-93.0)}
#'   \item{event}{Integer. Event indicator (0 = censored, 1 = event)}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_survival)
"jjscatterstats_survival"

#' General Tumour Biomarker Test Dataset
#'
#' The primary jjscatterstats test dataset: correlated tumour biomarkers with a
#' realistic amount of missing data, for testing complete-case handling alongside
#' the standard correlation paths.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 200 observations and 13 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{patient_id}{Integer. Unique patient identifier (1-200)}
#'   \item{ki67_index}{Numeric. Ki-67 proliferation index, percent (0-73.8)}
#'   \item{tumor_size}{Numeric. Tumour size, mm (10.0-105.7)}
#'   \item{protein_expression}{Numeric. Protein expression score (17.2-94.5); 6 missing values}
#'   \item{mutation_burden}{Numeric. Tumour mutational burden, mutations/Mb (0-34.0); 6 missing values}
#'   \item{immune_score}{Numeric. Composite immune infiltration score (0-129.9)}
#'   \item{age}{Numeric. Age in years (27-94)}
#'   \item{tumor_stage}{Character. Tumour stage}
#'   \item{tumor_grade}{Character. Histological grade}
#'   \item{receptor_status}{Character. Receptor status}
#'   \item{treatment_group}{Character. Treatment assignment}
#'   \item{response_score}{Numeric. Treatment response score (11.9-84.9)}
#'   \item{lymph_nodes}{Integer. Number of positive lymph nodes (0-18)}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_test)
"jjscatterstats_test"

#' Longitudinal Treatment Response Test Dataset
#'
#' Simulated repeated measurements on 75 patients across two timepoints, for
#' testing dose-response and biomarker-response correlations split by treatment
#' group or timepoint.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 150 observations and 11 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{patient_id}{Integer. Patient identifier (1-75; each appears at two timepoints)}
#'   \item{timepoint}{Character. Assessment timepoint}
#'   \item{drug_dose}{Numeric. Administered dose, mg (0-200)}
#'   \item{treatment_group}{Character. Treatment assignment}
#'   \item{age}{Numeric. Age in years (39-85)}
#'   \item{baseline_severity}{Numeric. Baseline disease severity score (25.7-99.4)}
#'   \item{tumor_size}{Numeric. Tumour size, mm (5.0-71.5)}
#'   \item{response_score}{Numeric. Treatment response score (0-100)}
#'   \item{biomarker_level}{Numeric. Circulating biomarker level (50-382)}
#'   \item{qol_score}{Numeric. Quality-of-life score (25.0-98.0)}
#'   \item{adverse_events}{Numeric. Number of adverse events (0-10)}
#' }
#' @docType data
#' @keywords datasets
#' @usage data(jjscatterstats_treatment)
"jjscatterstats_treatment"
